        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in cross stitch; strips of cotton have been stitched around the edges.\nThe black ground has a large flattened eight-pointed star in red, with a central beige quatrefoil shape (possibly representing a pool of water) within which are four floral motifs which may be flowers growing from a central island.  Around the 'pool' are four yellow stylised trees and four U-shapes which are filled with geometric motifs. In each corner of the cover is a stylised red palmette flanked by white leaf forms; these alternate with a large U-shaped motif in beige and with other scattered motifs. It is possible that this design represents a version of a Persian Garden Carpet. A narrow yellow border has a thin black angular meander carrying blue, red, yellow and green leaf forms. \nThere are some repairs using surface darning which may indicate that surface darning is a more recent technique.\nColours (Embroidery threads, 2S silk): white, beige, black, red, blue, green, yellow."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/fc3dba68-1d0e-3b8a-b39c-be0656351d9c> .

